# Topic 7 · Gender-Based Violence and the Three Case Studies

::: glance | Topic 7 at a glance
**Heads VIII and IX** of the syllabus: ==10.5 visits== (nine full questions and three short notes, 2016–2026), plus 12 of the 140 MCQs. Four families: **forms and strategies** (2016 sites and forms, 2017 workable strategies, 2023 practical strategies — three near repeats; 2024 the Punjab Act 2016 and consequences); **theory** (2020 power and control; 2025 root causes and how they intersect; 2026 note on masculinity studies); **law and honour** (2017 note on honour killing; 2018 note on government initiatives); and the **case studies** (Mukhtaran Mai 2019, Sharmeen Obaid-Chinoy 2020, Malala 2025). Every answer needs a definition, current data (PDHS, SSDO, HRCP), theory, the named forms or laws, and five-P strategies. Never yet asked in full: acid attacks, workplace harassment, cyber violence, the ecological model, a comparison of the three case studies.
:::

